--TEST--
A program's attribute on an enum, an enum case or a class constant is `E0874`, because a program's declaration cannot list those sites, and the same attribute on a class, a method and a property compiles — `rule:attributes/an-attribute-is-declared-with-its-sites`
--FILE--
<?nvs
attribute Label on class, method, property { text: string }

#[Label(text: "suit")]
enum Suit {
    #[Label(text: "hearts")]
    Hearts,
    Spades,
}

#[Label(text: "shop")]
class Shop {
    #[Label(text: "limit")]
    public const int LIMIT = 3;

    #[Label(text: "name")]
    public string $name = "";

    #[Label(text: "open")]
    public function open(): void {}
}

echo Shop::LIMIT, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0874]: `Label` is used on an enum, and its declaration allows only `class`, `method` and `property`
  --> case.nvs:4:3
%A
error[E0874]: `Label` is used on an enum case, and its declaration allows only `class`, `method` and `property`
  --> case.nvs:6:7
%A
error[E0874]: `Label` is used on a class constant, and its declaration allows only `class`, `method` and `property`
   --> case.nvs:13:7
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
